A||N||3||bHooper||Poly bushings and Caster question.||||1||
Z||000000||bHooper||11-08-2000||10:41 PM||||i am installing poly bushings, and have a question about the upper control arms.<P>the factory sets the castor with 2 6 mm washers (on the inner side of both halvs of the control arm)... however, when you install the poly bushings, it only allows room for one 6mm washer and a little extra.<P>so, what should i do?  do i install 7 1mm washers (8 if i can)?  <B>HELP!!</B><P>Thanks!<P>obtw, the poly rules!  i can't believe how tight things were on the lower control arms!... had to pound them suckers in!  together with the Eibachs, and despite the cheap Monroe shocks, this sucker is gonna be <B>AWESOME</B><P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/alien.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by bHooper (edited 11-09-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||11-09-2000||12:30 AM||||What year car are you installing them on? On my 86 SE I was able to install all the caster washer back into the control arms. <BR>You can buy a caster kit thru GM (Sunfire, Cavalier, Grand Am, etc all have the same size for the caster washers just different thickness'. I think the set goes from 2mm to 9mm) and I think MOOG make a set too. Even after replacing the original washers the alignment shop still had to change them since I switched to the poly and the eibach lowering springs. The alignment shop I went to carried there own master kit of caster washers for all types of cars.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 11-09-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||bHooper||11-09-2000||07:10 AM||||i corrected the washer thickness.<P>its my '86 GT.  i will know for sure, if i am able to work on it tonight.  sometimes if youi aproach things with a fresh mind, you get a different perspective (plus i will look at the drivers side).  but it really looked like there was no room there last night!<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/alien.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||11-09-2000||10:36 AM||||BHooper, If I remember correctly when I did mine I had to move the bushings out a bit to fit the washers in but when I torqued the long bolt, everything cinched up nicely.||||reg||1
